From: sidharthify <wednisegit@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] eventcontrollerkey: Keep IM focus while focus moves inside the widget

A search entry with a key capture widget puts its IM context on a key
controller of that widget, usually the whole window. When focus moves
between two children of the window, the controller sees the focus-out
crossing first and drops IM focus, then the focus-in crossing and takes
it back. On Wayland that ends up as text-input disable and enable in one
commit, which text-input v1 compositors read as a request to show the
on-screen keyboard, so the OSK pops up on every tap in apps like
GNOME Settings.

Keep IM focus when focus moves to another child of the widget, unless
the new focus is a text widget with its own IM context.

Signed-off-by: sidharthify <wednisegit@gmail.com>
---
--- a/gtk/gtkeventcontrollerkey.c
+++ b/gtk/gtkeventcontrollerkey.c
@@ -173,7 +173,13 @@
   is_focus = end_crossing ||
     /* Keep IM focused if focus moves from an input capture widget to the real one */
     (start_crossing &&
-     gtk_im_context_get_client_widget (key->im_context) == crossing->new_target);
+     gtk_im_context_get_client_widget (key->im_context) == crossing->new_target) ||
+    /* Keep IM focused if focus moves between children of the widget */
+    (start_crossing && crossing->new_target &&
+     (crossing->new_target == widget ||
+      gtk_widget_is_ancestor (crossing->new_target, widget)) &&
+     !GTK_IS_TEXT (crossing->new_target) &&
+     !GTK_IS_TEXT_VIEW (crossing->new_target));
 
   if (key->is_focus != is_focus)
     {
